{
  "name": "Validate and deduplicate webhook leads into Google Sheets with a review queue",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 1200,
        "content": "# Validate and deduplicate webhook leads into Google Sheets with a review queue\n\n## Who's it for\nAnyone piping form, webhook or lead data into a sheet or CRM who has been bitten by duplicate rows, records created from half-empty payloads, or data that quietly went missing without anyone noticing.\n\n## How it works\nA webhook receives the payload. A Set node normalizes it, trimming and lowercasing before anything is compared. An If node validates the required fields, and anything that fails is appended to a **Review Queue** tab together with the reason it failed, so bad records stay visible instead of being discarded. Valid records are looked up against an id the source system owns, and are only created if they are genuinely new. A retried webhook therefore becomes a no-op rather than a second row.\n\n## How to set up\n1. Add your Google Sheets credential to the three Google Sheets nodes.\n2. Put your spreadsheet ID into the **Settings** node.\n3. Create two tabs in that spreadsheet: `Records` and `Review Queue`.\n4. Point your source system at the production webhook URL.\n\n## Requirements\nA Google Sheets credential, and any source that can POST JSON.\n\n## How to customize\nSwap Google Sheets for your own CRM or database; the shape is what matters, not the storage. Adjust the rules in the **Valid?** node to match your required fields, and change `source_id` to whatever stable unique id your source provides."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Receive intake webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        -40,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "intake",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        180,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "name": "spreadsheetId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        120,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 280,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## Configure here\n\nPut your spreadsheet ID in the **Settings** node once. Every Google Sheets node below reads it from there, so there is only one place to change."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Normalize fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        400,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "name": "email",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($('Receive intake webhook').item.json.body?.email ?? '').toString().trim().toLowerCase() }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f2",
              "name": "name",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($('Receive intake webhook').item.json.body?.name ?? '').toString().trim() }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f3",
              "name": "source_id",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($('Receive intake webhook').item.json.body?.id ?? '').toString().trim() }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "f4",
              "name": "received_at",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Normalize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        420,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## Normalize before comparing\n\n`  Bob@Example.com ` and `bob@example.com` are the same person, but a deduplication check treats them as two different ones unless you trim and lowercase first.\n\nThis one step removes a large share of duplicate records on its own."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Valid?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        640,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "regex"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.email }}",
              "rightValue": "^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$"
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.source_id }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Append to review queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        900,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "name": "={{ $json.name }}",
            "email": "={{ $json.email }}",
            "reason": "={{ !$json.email.match(/^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$/) ? 'invalid or missing email' : 'missing source_id' }}",
            "source_id": "={{ $json.source_id }}",
            "received_at": "={{ $json.received_at }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Review Queue"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.spreadsheetId }}"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Review queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        850,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Invalid records go to a queue, not to nowhere\n\nThe common shortcut is a filter that silently drops anything malformed. The workflow keeps reporting success while records quietly disappear.\n\nRouting failures to a review tab costs one node, and it means a person can see what failed and why. A blank required field should be flagged, never quietly guessed at."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Look up existing by source id",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        900,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "operation": "lookup",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Records"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.spreadsheetId }}"
        },
        "lookupValue": "={{ $json.source_id }}",
        "lookupColumn": "source_id"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7,
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Deduplicate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        850,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## Deduplicate on an id the source owns\n\nUse the upstream system's own id, not a timestamp and not a row number.\n\nWhen a webhook is retried, and eventually it will be, the retry carries the **same** source id but a **new** timestamp. Deduplicate on time and you create the record twice.\n\nThis node is set to always output data and to continue on error, so that finding no match returns an empty item instead of halting the run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "New record?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        1160,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "d1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "empty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.source_id }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
      "name": "Create record",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        1400,
        100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "name": "={{ $('Normalize fields').item.json.name }}",
            "email": "={{ $('Normalize fields').item.json.email }}",
            "source_id": "={{ $('Normalize fields').item.json.source_id }}",
            "received_at": "={{ $('Normalize fields').item.json.received_at }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Records"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.spreadsheetId }}"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014",
      "name": "Duplicate, skip",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "position": [
        1400,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Endings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1350,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## Two endings, both deliberate\n\n**Create record** means it is genuinely new, so write it.\n\n**Duplicate, skip** means it has been seen before, so do nothing. This branch exists on purpose: a retry should be a no-op, not an error and not a second row.\n\nIf you need to prove later that a retry was handled, replace the No Operation node with a log row instead."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
